Overview & Objective

Develop a small VR application using Unity and the Meta All-in-One SDK that demonstrates key interaction systems, hand tracking, UI, animations, and core gameplay mechanics.

Technical Requirements

Engine: Unity 2022.3 LTS or Unity 6

SDK: Meta All-in-One SDK

Target Hardware: Meta Quest 3 / Quest 3S / Quest Pro

Language: C#

Functional Requirements

Hand Tracking & Controllers

Support both Hand Tracking and Touch Controllers with seamless auto-switching.

Configure Hand Grab Snap Poses for all interactable objects.

Object Interaction

Create three grabbable and throwable objects: Cube, Sphere, and Cylinder.

Configure hand snap poses for each object.

Implement auto-return to original position if an object is dropped outside the designated target zone.

Placement Puzzle Mechanics

Create three distinct target sockets (one matching each shape).

Enforce object-to-socket validation (prevent incorrect placements).

On Incorrect Placement: Display an explicit error message.

On Correct Placement: Snap object into place, disable further grabbing, trigger a success audio cue, and change socket color to green.

On Puzzle Completion (All 3 placed): Trigger a door opening animation and display a "Task Completed" message.

World Space UI

Floating dashboard displaying: Objects Remaining count, Timer, Reset Button, and Restart Button.

Wrist-Mounted Hand Menu

Menu anchored to the wrist containing options to: Reset Scene, Restart Task, and Toggle Hand Tracking Visualization.

Interaction Feedback & Audio/Haptics

Highlight objects on hover.

Visual and audio feedback for Hover, Grab, Place, Wrong Placement, and Completion.

Haptic feedback for controller interactions.

Environment Setup

Create a simple room environment containing a table, lighting, a door, a placement area, and an instruction board.

Animations & Polish

Door opening animation, object snap animation, and UI fade-in/fade-out transitions.

Performance & Code Quality

Target and maintain a stable 72+ FPS on Meta Quest.

Clean prefab and script organization; avoid unnecessary Update() calls.

Bonus Features (Optional)

Two-handed grab interaction.

Hand pinch gesture to reset the scene.

Voice instruction playback upon task initiation.

Particle effect burst upon correct object placement.

Local progress saving/restoration across app restarts.